=2 Walkthrough
* Speak to {n:Octavernost} (K-9) near the Big Bridge waypoint in {z:Western Adoulin} as a Rune Fencer.
** Unlike the previous requirement of having the full set of Artifact for being able to start commissioning Runefencer Relic armor. You only need to have obtained one piece of the armor. However, trying to skip on quests up to relic armor by using {i:Kupon A-AF +3} to flag this quest will not work.
** This isn't the same NPC who gives you the Rune Fencer quest.
* Head to {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar} (M-6) and check the Meeting Point for a cutscene and to receive a {k:Refined Ra'Kaznar fiber} key item.
** This spot is close to the enigmatic waypoint warp.
* Return to {n:Octavernost}. He will offer you three KIs which allow you into three different fights of different difficulties. These are solo fights you must face as Rune Fencer.
** {k:Iridal core of the tomb} is a level 109 fight in {z:King Ranperre's Tomb}.
** {k:Iridal core of the ruins} is a level 125 fight in {z:Fei'Yin}.
** The blank option will give you the {k:Iridal core of the pass}. This is a level 135 fight in {z:Ranguemont Pass}.

=4 Iridal core of the tomb - King Ranperre's Tomb - 109
* Head to {z:King Ranperre's Tomb} (H-10) and examine the **???** in the middle of the concrete slab to enter Map 2.
* Then proceed along the right wall to the NW corner (E-8) and run through the fake wall. Examine the **Hazy Rune** behind the {q:Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus}.
** Check it once again to begin the fight.
*** Buffs and TP are reset as the fight begins.
**** Food, and for whatever reason, {p:Vallation} / {p:Valiance} are not lost.
*** You may summon {p:Trusts|Trust} to assist you.
*** You may change jobs for this fight.

The fight is against an {p:Animated Weapon|Category:Animated Weapon} named **{m:Arcus Blades}**.
* It has very low HP, but will cast dispelga and various single target elemental magic tier IV-VI. The tier VI are capable of one shotting you or your trusts.
** See the monster's page for more information.

* After defeating {m:Arcus Blades} you will earn 10,000 {p:Bayld}, and your {k:Refined Ra'Kaznar fiber} will transform into an {k:Arcus fiber}.
* Proceed to the "Afterwards" section below.

=4 Iridal core of the ruins - Fei'Yin - 125
* Proceed to {z:Fei'Yin} (G-9) to cross over to Map 2.
* Head to (E-7) to cross back over to Map 1.
* Go to (G-6) and examine the **Hazy Rune** behind the {q:Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus}.
** Check it once again to begin the fight.
*** Buffs and TP are reset as the fight begins.
**** Food, and for whatever reason, {p:Vallation} / {p:Valiance} are not lost.
*** You may summon {p:Trusts|Trust} to assist you.
*** You may change jobs for this fight.

 The fight is against an {p:Animated Weapon|Category:Animated Weapon} named **{m:Arcus Blades}**.
* It has very low HP, but will cast dispelga and various single target elemental magic tier IV-VI. The tier VI are capable of one shotting you or your trusts.
** See the monster's page for more information.

* After defeating {m:Arcus Blades} you will earn 3 synthesis materials related to the {p:Erilaz Armor Set}.

* Proceed to the "Afterwards" section below.

=4 Iridal core of the pass - Ranguemont Pass - 135
* Make your way to the {q:Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus} in {z:Ranguemont Pass}.
* Examine the **Hazy Rune** behind the {q:Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus|Strange Apparatus}.
** Check it once again to begin the fight.
*** Buffs and TP are reset as the fight begins.
**** Food, and for whatever reason, {p:Vallation} / {p:Valiance} are not lost.
* You may **not** summon {p:Trusts|Trust} to assist you.
* You must be on RUN for this fight.

The fight is against an {p:Animated Weapon|Category:Animated Weapon} named **{m:Arcus Blades}**.
* It has very low HP, but will cast dispelga and various single target elemental magic tier IV-VI. The tier VI are capable of one shotting you.
** See the monster's page for more information.
** See the {p:discussion|Talk:Epiphany} page for strategies and testimonials.

* After defeating {m:Arcus Blades} you will earn 10 synthesis materials related to the {p:Erilaz Armor Set} and a {i:Codex of Etchings|Codex of Etchings|6367}.
* You also earn the title **Sword Saint** and {n:Octavernost} will address you as such.

* Proceed to the "Afterwards" section below.

=4 Afterwards
* **Optional:** Return to {n:Octavernost} at the Big Bridge who instructs you to proceed to Amchuchu.
* Check **Amchuchu's Laboratory** at the Inventor's Coalition in {z:Western Adoulin} (J-10) for a cutsene.
* Wait one game day and then talk to {n:Octavernost} for your reward of 15000 {p:XP} and an {i:Erilaz Surcoat|Erilaz Surcoat|26940}!
* You may speak to {n:Octavernost} afterwards to request another KI to repeat a fight.
** This may be done once per conquest tally.

=2 The Rest of the Armor
* After receiving your Surcoat you may immediately speak with {n:Octavernost} to begin forging the rest of the {p:Erilaz Armor Set}.
** You do not need to zone, and do not need to be on RUN to forge the rest of the set.
** You can only forge one piece of armor per game day.
* He will ask for different ingredients for each piece of armor; after trading the ingredients he will give you a {@k} Order slip for the armor. You must wait until the next game day to receive the armor.
** If you have completed Part 1 of {q:Quiescence|Quiescence|Quiescence} (Ergon Weapon Quest) {n:Octavernost} will only ask for an {i:Isgebind's Heart|Isgebind's Heart|3290} or half as many {i:H-P Bayld|H-P Bayld|8798} (rounded down).

